WEBVTT

00:06.030 --> 00:10.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:06.030 --> 00:10.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:10.630 --> 00:18.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:10.630 --> 00:18.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:18.610 --> 00:22.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:18.610 --> 00:22.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:23.210 --> 00:28.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:23.210 --> 00:28.900
I just want to be someone who

00:28.900 --> 00:33.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:28.900 --> 00:33.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

00:33.460 --> 00:39.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

00:33.460 --> 00:39.800
I want to get excited for it!

00:40.330 --> 00:44.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

00:40.330 --> 00:44.860
So I step out, unstoppable

00:44.860 --> 00:49.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

00:44.860 --> 00:49.450
And take everything into my own hands

00:49.940 --> 00:54.050
sono saki de aitai

00:49.940 --> 00:54.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

00:54.050 --> 01:00.040
mita koto no nai atashi

00:54.050 --> 01:00.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:00.510 --> 01:05.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:00.510 --> 01:05.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:05.160 --> 01:09.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:05.160 --> 01:09.710
I'll try to do my best

01:09.710 --> 01:17.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:09.710 --> 01:17.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:22.390 --> 01:26.840
Situation 11

01:22.390 --> 01:26.840
Deadly Battle! Guard Duty of the
Ibaragi Prefecture Exhibition

01:26.840 --> 01:34.590
Ibaraki Prefecture Governor
Ichihashi Kuniko

01:26.860 --> 01:30.650
We will open the exhibition as originally planned.

01:30.650 --> 01:39.370
If any citizens sustain injuries, we will hold the Ministry of Justice and the Media Cleansing Committee responsible.

01:39.600 --> 01:42.570
You're not going to hold the Library Force responsible?

01:42.570 --> 01:46.450
The Library Force is providing protection at our request,

01:46.450 --> 01:52.590
so the only thing we'd hold them responsible for is if they were unable to protect the exhibit.

01:52.590 --> 01:57.800
Taking the safety of the citizens into consideration, would it not be better to delay or cancel the exhibit?

01:57.800 --> 02:03.020
The root problem is that the central government is interfering with the prefecture's citizen's celebration of the arts.

02:03.020 --> 02:04.380
Well said!

02:04.380 --> 02:07.210
Both the art museum curator and the governor have guts.

02:07.210 --> 02:08.630
This is encouraging.

02:08.630 --> 02:12.290
But I'm disappointed that the press is siding with the Media Cleansing Committee.

02:12.290 --> 02:13.450
Don't complain.

02:13.450 --> 02:15.000
They're striking a balance that way.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.160
But...

02:16.160 --> 02:17.430
Look, Kasahara.

02:23.470 --> 02:26.810
Dad's fighting with me.

02:30.110 --> 02:31.140
Sorry.

02:31.140 --> 02:32.160
I'll step out.

02:39.390 --> 02:41.350
I saw the press conference.

02:41.350 --> 02:44.490
Did LSTC Genda write the script?

02:44.490 --> 02:45.990
That's none of your business.

02:45.990 --> 02:47.860
Don't give me the cold shoulder.

02:47.860 --> 02:50.570
I'm concerned about Mito.

02:51.070 --> 02:53.670
Your superiors are quite sharp.

02:53.670 --> 02:55.550
Yes, I admire them.

02:55.880 --> 03:00.680
In paying him my respects, I'll tell you some information I have.

03:00.680 --> 03:05.520
The censorship this time will only be attempted once. It'll be on the first day of the exhibit, before the opening.

03:05.520 --> 03:07.010
Only once?

03:07.010 --> 03:13.960
The Media Cleansing Committee is getting very emotional about this year's choice work.

03:13.960 --> 03:17.620
As someone who wears a uniform, you should know.

03:18.010 --> 03:19.020
Yeah.

03:19.020 --> 03:21.450
But the Ministry of Justice isn't enthusiastic about it.

03:21.450 --> 03:26.680
The local government is taking a hard-line stance, so we don't want to make any trouble.

03:26.680 --> 03:31.680
This censorship is all about the pride of the Media Cleansing Committee.

03:31.680 --> 03:33.600
Is it really only going to be once?

03:33.600 --> 03:37.110
It's up to you to believe me or not.

03:37.110 --> 03:39.240
Thanks for telling me.

03:39.240 --> 03:42.020
I at least appreciate the information.

03:42.020 --> 03:43.080
Hikaru,

03:44.470 --> 03:48.590
am I being horrible to you?

03:48.590 --> 03:51.090
No, you don't have to answer that.

04:00.080 --> 04:07.180
As you guessed, the Non-Violence Club had close financial ties to groups siding with the Media Cleansing Committee.

04:07.180 --> 04:08.350
Yes.

04:08.350 --> 04:15.860
The Library Force at the Mito Station was most likely systematically made powerless by the Media Cleansing Committee.

04:18.450 --> 04:20.510
I see.

04:20.510 --> 04:23.090
Thank you for looking everything up.

04:23.090 --> 04:27.200
Can you keep this information hidden from the members on site?

04:27.200 --> 04:28.530
Yes.

04:28.530 --> 04:33.490
I don't want to give them any information that would lower their morale.

04:48.480 --> 04:49.730
Tezuka, it was right on.

04:49.730 --> 04:54.110
The notice says that the censorship is limited to one time only, in front of the building, right before the opening of the exhibit on the first day.

04:54.110 --> 04:58.890
The notice has the signature of the Minister of Justice, too.

04:58.890 --> 05:00.950
There will be no ambush.

05:00.950 --> 05:02.780
That's a relief.

05:02.780 --> 05:08.000
Considering the skill level of the local force, a prolonged situation would be difficult for us.

05:08.000 --> 05:10.570
Your brother's information was right.

05:10.570 --> 05:12.420
But it wasn't useful.

05:12.420 --> 05:13.460
Oh, come on!

05:14.120 --> 05:17.560
The plan of action for a short battle scenario is ready.

05:17.560 --> 05:21.820
Without the information from your brother, we couldn't have prepared it so quickly.

05:21.820 --> 05:24.500
That's great to hear.

05:24.500 --> 05:25.970
I'll explain the formation.

05:25.970 --> 05:27.430
Put down what you're working on and listen.

05:28.490 --> 05:31.820
The Cleansing Force's target is this year's prize work, Freiheit.

05:31.820 --> 05:35.780
We will isolate it to avoid damage to other works.

05:35.780 --> 05:39.280
We will put it in a bulletproof case and set it outside.

05:39.280 --> 05:42.040
We will enclose the campus using cars.

05:42.040 --> 05:46.780
We will fill the gaps with barricades, and we will use this spot to get in and out.

05:46.780 --> 05:49.380
On the library side that's carrying the pamphlets,

05:49.380 --> 05:52.340
we'll station the force that's made up by primarily local members.

05:52.340 --> 05:55.000
Ogata, you take command here.

05:55.000 --> 05:56.340
Yes, Sir.

05:56.340 --> 05:59.390
The combat will end at 9 in the morning.

05:59.390 --> 06:02.350
Don't let the Cleansing Force step in until then.

06:02.350 --> 06:03.210
That's all!

06:03.210 --> 06:04.300
Yes, Sir!

06:08.330 --> 06:10.330
I should use one size bigger.

06:10.330 --> 06:12.270
Dojo, I'll stand guard for a bit.

06:12.270 --> 06:14.730
You should rest for a while.

06:14.730 --> 06:17.740
Thank you.

06:17.740 --> 06:20.230
You there! It'll topple over easily if you stack them like that!

06:21.220 --> 06:23.630
Everyone seems tired.

06:23.630 --> 06:25.740
Should I go buy something for everyone?

06:25.740 --> 06:27.470
That'd be great.

06:27.470 --> 06:28.140
Keep it up.

06:28.140 --> 06:29.440
Put an XL here.

06:29.440 --> 06:30.930
Yes, Sir.

06:30.930 --> 06:32.200
Instructor Dojo...

06:33.980 --> 06:38.650
There's a place I want to take you, if you don't mind.

06:57.950 --> 06:59.270
Come in.

06:59.270 --> 07:00.240
Okay.

07:06.860 --> 07:08.340
What is it?

07:08.340 --> 07:11.790
You said you wanted to see them blooming.

07:11.790 --> 07:13.610
Are these chamomiles?

07:25.050 --> 07:26.130
You...

07:40.260 --> 07:42.000
They smell great.

07:42.000 --> 07:46.900
I think whoever planted these here also knows the meanings flowers have.

07:47.630 --> 07:49.750
Energy in adversity, huh...

07:50.210 --> 07:57.710
I think there's someone who believes that the base will be better one day, even though he or she is treated unfairly today.

07:58.980 --> 08:00.750
Right.

08:01.460 --> 08:04.960
I'll do my best for these people, too.

08:07.300 --> 08:10.530
I'm not a rookie anymore, so I will give my best as a member of—

08:10.530 --> 08:11.680
Kasahara...

08:14.290 --> 08:17.660
I didn't expect to see you here.

08:17.660 --> 08:22.420
They're docking my pay for three months because of what happened.

08:22.420 --> 08:28.930
A Library Force member and a Cleansing Force member shouldn't be talking needlessly, even in private.

08:28.930 --> 08:33.340
We'll be shooting at each other when the night is over.

08:33.340 --> 08:37.300
One of us might die, and we won't be able to talk ever again.

08:41.290 --> 08:44.780
I like brilliant people like you.

08:44.780 --> 08:47.510
The Cleansing Force is full of idiots.

08:47.510 --> 08:50.810
Then why don't you switch sides to the Library Force?

08:50.810 --> 08:53.800
One of my superior officers was in the Cleansing Force once.

08:53.800 --> 08:57.450
I was hired through a personal connection, so I can't.

08:59.440 --> 09:03.230
Unlike you, we have no ambition.

09:03.230 --> 09:09.800
All we have are personal connections like me, people just looking to be promoted, or career soldiers.

09:12.580 --> 09:15.530
But this time, we're getting excited.

09:15.530 --> 09:17.200
Be careful.

09:17.200 --> 09:18.660
Freiheit...

09:20.370 --> 09:22.100
According to the information from Tezuka,

09:22.100 --> 09:28.140
the Cleansing Force is getting emotional because they thought they were disgraced by it.

09:28.140 --> 09:32.390
I'm sure their pride will be on the line in tomorrow's battle.

09:33.080 --> 09:35.350
The Cleansing Force's pride...

09:35.830 --> 09:40.150
You never know what people will do in that kind of situation.

09:40.150 --> 09:41.540
The battle tomorrow...

09:44.610 --> 09:50.570
The battle tomorrow will be far worse than the one at Odawara.

09:51.290 --> 09:57.750
They have no ambition, but they have an intense sense of pride in their organization.

09:57.750 --> 10:00.870
I guess they can't dismiss that artwork.

10:00.870 --> 10:02.550
You guess?

10:02.550 --> 10:05.640
I don't carry any such worthless pride.

10:05.640 --> 10:11.250
Censorship itself is done in defense of some higher-ups.

10:11.250 --> 10:15.590
I'm not willing to risk my life for such a reason.

10:26.870 --> 10:32.640
If they break the agreement and start attacking blindly...

10:32.640 --> 10:36.250
I may fail as a superior officer to say this,

10:37.800 --> 10:40.520
but prioritize saving your life.

10:42.700 --> 10:43.960
Sir...

10:52.590 --> 10:54.180
I won't hear any excuses!

10:54.180 --> 10:58.300
I'll ask you to do a follow-up on the situation once we're done here.

10:58.300 --> 11:00.340
It's not my fault...

11:00.340 --> 11:01.970
It's not...

11:23.350 --> 11:24.370
They're here.

11:46.520 --> 11:48.940
Fire at will!

11:50.590 --> 11:51.850
Permission to fire!

11:52.290 --> 11:54.120
Fire!

12:10.480 --> 12:11.440
The next group's coming.

12:11.440 --> 12:13.030
In the bush to the south!

12:13.030 --> 12:13.900
Roger.

12:18.390 --> 12:19.440
Let's go!

12:19.440 --> 12:20.700
LOFC Shindo!

12:21.370 --> 12:22.800
LOFC Shindo is hit!

12:22.800 --> 12:23.960
What?!

12:23.960 --> 12:25.370
It went through his upper arm.

12:25.370 --> 12:26.940
He's unable to remain on duty!

12:26.940 --> 12:28.240
Where was he shot from?

12:36.720 --> 12:37.470
In the trees!

12:37.470 --> 12:41.270
It's not as high as the roof, but they can shoot at the snipers leaning out.

12:41.270 --> 12:46.650
Up on the tallest tree, they must be on the highest branches that you can climb!

12:46.650 --> 12:47.970
All right.

12:47.970 --> 12:50.890
I'm counting on you, Mr. Afraid-of-Heights Sniper.

12:50.890 --> 12:52.710
I've overcome my fear for some time now.

12:54.180 --> 12:55.440
In the tree, huh...

12:55.440 --> 12:56.600
Tezuka, can you do it?

12:56.600 --> 12:57.630
I can.

12:57.630 --> 12:58.950
I'll be the decoy.

12:58.950 --> 13:00.660
You go downstairs.

13:00.660 --> 13:02.240
I'll take a few shots from them,

13:02.240 --> 13:04.930
and find their locations from their bullet traces.

13:05.530 --> 13:07.140
Can you shoot with your arm like that?

13:07.510 --> 13:09.720
As long as I don't have to hit them.

13:09.720 --> 13:12.210
But you must take each one down with a single shot.

13:12.210 --> 13:13.560
No room for mistakes.

13:13.560 --> 13:14.610
Roger.

13:15.060 --> 13:16.150
One on that tree...

13:19.250 --> 13:20.810
Another one.

13:20.810 --> 13:23.950
I won't make LOFC Shindo shoot any more!

13:29.880 --> 13:31.740
You've improved.

13:31.740 --> 13:33.210
Not really.

13:34.230 --> 13:36.870
I thought you'd need four or five more shots.

13:36.870 --> 13:39.430
I'm not <i>that</i> bad either.

13:39.820 --> 13:41.390
The enemy's snipers are down.

13:41.390 --> 13:44.700
LOFC Shindo and CL Tezuka are heading to an aid station.

13:44.700 --> 13:46.970
Send Komaki in place of Shindo.

13:46.970 --> 13:48.400
Put Tezuka back, too.

13:49.040 --> 13:50.240
This place is yours now.

13:50.240 --> 13:51.660
O-Okay!

13:55.310 --> 13:56.770
Shoot, idiots!

13:56.770 --> 13:59.800
They'll focus their fire here if they find that this is our weak spot!

14:00.110 --> 14:02.820
Always replenish your bullets after you use half of your clip.

14:02.820 --> 14:04.480
They'll focus their aim there if you run out.

14:04.480 --> 14:05.720
O-Okay!

14:08.260 --> 14:09.300
Kasahara!

14:09.300 --> 14:13.980
Ask the Captain to send a member of the Task Force here, whoever is available!

14:13.980 --> 14:15.000
Yes, Sir!

14:17.770 --> 14:18.870
The machine's down!

14:18.870 --> 14:19.980
I'll make a run for it!

14:19.980 --> 14:21.010
H-Hey!

14:28.080 --> 14:29.150
You're asking for the impossible!

14:29.150 --> 14:30.580
We're shorthanded everywhere!

14:30.580 --> 14:31.670
Refill!

14:30.980 --> 14:31.670
But!

14:31.670 --> 14:32.680
No buts!

14:32.680 --> 14:35.090
Refill! Refill! Refill!

14:35.090 --> 14:36.740
You guys...

14:37.600 --> 14:39.600
You brought these here?

14:39.600 --> 14:42.060
Because all the guys were out.

14:42.060 --> 14:43.170
Great work!

14:48.900 --> 14:51.120
30 minutes until the end of the battle.

15:00.470 --> 15:04.070
The Cleansing Force members from the library section are coming over to join the members here!

15:04.070 --> 15:05.010
What?!

15:05.010 --> 15:08.280
The enemy is focusing their force on the museum side.

15:09.790 --> 15:11.690
Gather all the riot shields here!

15:12.710 --> 15:15.520
If they're not enough, use steel plates, or whatever!

15:15.520 --> 15:17.400
Strengthen the barricade!

15:22.320 --> 15:23.560
Hey!

15:23.560 --> 15:24.600
You all right?

15:26.550 --> 15:29.000
They're out of control.

15:29.000 --> 15:32.210
The Cleansing Force's attack is in its final stage.

15:32.210 --> 15:35.720
They're using their downed members as a shield to push their way in!

15:43.650 --> 15:45.700
Don't hesitate to shoot at close range!

15:45.700 --> 15:50.010
Make disarming them and protecting your lives top priority!

15:51.740 --> 15:53.280
Carry the injured inside the museum!

15:57.230 --> 15:59.630
Kasahara! Get yourself inside!

15:59.630 --> 16:01.050
I refuse!

16:02.740 --> 16:03.510
Kasahara!

16:03.510 --> 16:05.600
I'm your messenger.

16:05.600 --> 16:08.240
I'm staying with you until the end!

16:09.230 --> 16:11.180
You idiot!

16:12.310 --> 16:13.560
Don't let them through!

16:13.560 --> 16:14.650
Push them back!

16:14.650 --> 16:15.460
I'll take over here!

16:15.460 --> 16:16.470
Please!

16:36.590 --> 16:41.530
Are you telling me there are things you must take away, even doing this?

16:42.850 --> 16:44.330
Why?

16:56.620 --> 16:58.250
Stay away!

17:17.480 --> 17:18.430
Huh?

17:18.430 --> 17:19.610
Why?

17:19.610 --> 17:20.410
Go in!

17:20.410 --> 17:21.770
Go in! Go in!

17:23.630 --> 17:25.620
Thank you for saving me.

17:25.620 --> 17:28.650
The Cleansing Force members that CL Kasahara shot are retreating.

17:28.650 --> 17:33.700
Shooting men in bulletproof vests with weakened bullets won't kill them so easily.

17:33.700 --> 17:34.780
Calm down!

17:54.850 --> 17:56.350
Don't worry about it.

17:56.350 --> 17:59.500
Everyone's like that the first time they shoot someone.

18:00.170 --> 18:02.060
Tezuka was calm.

18:02.060 --> 18:03.220
He didn't shoot as many.

18:05.330 --> 18:06.890
Kasahara,

18:06.890 --> 18:09.390
if this is frustrating, then become strong!

18:09.390 --> 18:14.600
Train yourself so you'll always be calm under any circumstances, and not overcome by your emotions.

18:16.000 --> 18:19.060
It might be a difficult task for you.

18:19.060 --> 18:21.150
I can do it! I swear!

18:24.220 --> 18:29.870
You really took me by surprise when you said you'd stay with me because you're my messenger.

18:30.290 --> 18:31.540
I did?

18:40.270 --> 18:41.690
Stay here.

18:41.690 --> 18:42.580
Okay...

18:46.420 --> 18:48.340
Thank you for protecting it.

18:48.340 --> 18:48.900
No problem.

18:48.900 --> 18:51.860
It looks like there were many injuries.

18:51.860 --> 18:54.180
The Cleansing Force probably took more damage than we did.

18:54.180 --> 18:55.790
Move out of there!

19:00.540 --> 19:01.960
Everyone, hit the floor!

19:03.290 --> 19:06.680
The work you're after is behind me.

19:06.680 --> 19:09.180
Shoot if you dare.

19:30.060 --> 19:32.040
What are you doing there?

19:32.040 --> 19:35.950
The library gets ravaged because this is here.

19:35.950 --> 19:38.010
As long as it's gone...

19:38.010 --> 19:41.420
What you're doing is exactly what's ravaging the library!

19:41.420 --> 19:42.640
Shut up!

19:42.640 --> 19:46.020
Who do you think will be asked to take responsibility for this whole thing?!

19:46.020 --> 19:49.000
Nobody will accuse you for fighting against the censorship!

19:49.000 --> 19:52.840
If you give in to the censorship and burn the documents that we're supposed to protect,

19:52.840 --> 19:55.370
that would be the worst mistake of your life!

19:55.370 --> 19:57.080
Shut up!

19:57.080 --> 20:00.080
We just need to stay nonresistant to the censorships.

20:02.750 --> 20:04.350
Don't do it!

20:21.630 --> 20:25.070
Is that all you've got?

20:31.750 --> 20:34.000
Genda-san! Genda-san!

20:36.530 --> 20:38.150
Instructor Dojo!

20:38.150 --> 20:39.840
Kasahara! Capture the curator!

20:48.190 --> 20:49.480
Instructor...

20:59.910 --> 21:02.400
Instructor Dojo!

21:06.790 --> 21:10.130
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.790 --> 21:10.130
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.130 --> 21:13.510
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.130 --> 21:13.510
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.510 --> 21:18.520
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.510 --> 21:18.520
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.180 --> 21:26.860
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.180 --> 21:26.860
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.860 --> 21:36.530
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.860 --> 21:36.530
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.980 --> 21:40.510
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.980 --> 21:40.510
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.510 --> 21:43.830
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.510 --> 21:43.830
Goodbye my old self

21:43.830 --> 21:50.360
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.830 --> 21:50.360
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.360 --> 21:54.100
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.360 --> 21:54.100
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:54.100 --> 21:57.330
ushinau mono mo aru

21:54.100 --> 21:57.330
There are things I'll lose too

21:57.330 --> 22:03.100
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

21:57.330 --> 22:03.100
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

22:03.100 --> 22:10.650
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

22:03.100 --> 22:10.650
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

22:10.650 --> 22:20.940
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

22:10.650 --> 22:20.940
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
